Let me pull the read-only configuration for these three resources (and anything connected to them — network, backups, encryption keys) in eu-central-1.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_hQaIuQpoQqTdbAPH9pmwo3", "tool_name": "gather_context", "input": {"prompt": "{
  "task": "Gather read-only resilience/DR configuration data for a workload in eu-central-1 made of three named resources: RDS/Aurora MySQL instance or cluster 'dr-demo-mysql', ElastiCache (Valkey) replication group 'dr-demo-valkey', and DynamoDB table 'dr-demo-players'. Also check whether this workload is already registered in AWS Resilience Hub (next generation), and check shared dependencies (network/VPC AZs these resources use, KMS keys, backups).",
  "context": "User wants to start a disaster recovery assessment: DR for a Region failure or loss of one of these three services. They have no RPO/RTO yet. I am following the resilience-review skill's method (Steps 0, 2, 5) and need DATA ONLY back, not a prose assessment -- I will write the final report myself. Return one row per resource using this exact schema: layer | resource | type | Region | in-Region redundancy (AZs, nodes, tasks) | backups (kind, frequency, retention) | copies, images or IaC outside the Region | point-in-time recovery | replication | what could not be read. Also separately report: (a) Resilience Hub ListServices result in eu-central-1 (is this workload already a Resilience Hub service - match by name/resources), (b) any CloudFormation stack, resource-group, or tag (app/application/service/project/workload) that links these three resources together or to other resources (e.g. compute, load balancer) -- list as possible workload members, do not sweep the whole account, (c) AWS Backup: any backup plan/protected-resource entries and actual recovery points for these three resources, and whether DynamoDB advanced features are enabled in AWS Backup region settings, (d) KMS: whether these resources are encrypted and with which key (customer-managed vs AWS-managed), (e) network: which AZs/subnets these resources are deployed into.",
  "resources": ["dr-demo-mysql (RDS/Aurora)", "dr-demo-valkey (ElastiCache Valkey replication group)", "dr-demo-players (DynamoDB table)", "eu-central-1"],
  "timeframe": "current state (not time-bounded)",
  "criteria": "For RDS: DescribeDBInstances (or DescribeDBClusters if Aurora) for MultiAZ, BackupRetentionPeriod, ReadReplicaDBInstanceIdentifiers, DeletionProtection, StorageEncrypted, KmsKeyId; DescribeDBSnapshots; DescribeGlobalClusters if Aurora. For ElastiCache: DescribeReplicationGroups for AutomaticFailover, MultiAZ, number of member clusters/replicas, SnapshotRetentionLimit, GlobalReplicationGroupInfo, node type/family; DescribeSnapshots. For DynamoDB: DescribeContinuousBackups (PointInTimeRecoveryStatus, RecoveryPeriodInDays), ListBackups, DescribeTable (Replicas for global table) -- if DescribeTable is blocked, note it and rely on DescribeContinuousBackups/ListBackups. For Resilience Hub: resiliencehubv2 ListServices in eu-central-1, GetService if a match is found. For AWS Backup: ListBackupPlans, ListProtectedResources, ListRecoveryPointsByResource for each of the three resources, DescribeRegionSettings. Record every denied or empty call explicitly as 'not checked' with the reason -- do not report an empty result as 'no gap'."
}", "deep_research": true}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Gathering DR-relevant config for RDS, ElastiCache, and DynamoDB resources in eu-central-1."}], "created_at": null}

